<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Brunkeberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1471">1471</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Brunkeberg was fought on 10 October 1471 on a ridge outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a>, where the Swedish regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sten-sture-the-elder">Sten Sture the Elder</a>, with peasants, miners and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a>, defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-i-of-denmark">Christian I of Denmark</a>, who sought to enforce his rule over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a>. The victory secured Sture's regency and became a lasting symbol of Swedish independence from Danish rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-brunkeberg.jpg" alt="Battle of Brunkeberg" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georg von Rosen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Entry_of_Sten_Sture_the_Elder_into_Stockholm_(Georg_von_Rosen)_-_Nationalmuseum_-_19214.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
